is more about the parents' beliefs, which is a key point in the text. Option D is more about the scope of reading. Since the text discusses both the benefits and the habits, but the main focus is on the parents' agreement, A seems more fitting. However, D is also a strong contender because it points out that reading isn't just about books, which is an important observation in the context.\n\nWait, the text does mention that 30% of parents read with their children, which is a specific point, but the main theme is about the value and habits. So, the most suitable title would probably be one that captures the value aspect, which is A. Alternatively, D emphasizes the broader impact of reading, which is also a key point.\n\nI think the correct answer is A because it directly addresses the parents' agreement with the value of reading, which is the main point of the survey. D is also correct but more about the scope of reading beyond books, which is a secondary point.\n</think>\n\nThe correct option is: A",
