mental data in order to achieve political success.\" The context mentions that local departments might be indifferent or turn a blind eye, but it doesn't specifically say they whitewash data for political reasons. It talks about data bleaching but not whitewashing. So D might not be a direct statement either.\n\nPutting it all together, the context supports the idea that cracking down on fraud requires more than just punishing companies, which is exactly what option B states. So B is the intended statement.\n</think>\n\nThe correct option is: B\n\nThe reasoning is that option B directly reflects the context by stating that cracking down on environmental data fraud should involve more than just punishing the companies, aligning with the discussed chain of responsibility.\n\nThe correct option is: B",
