on C: This talks about a supermarket needing security guards based on size. If a supermarket uses three guards, it must be big. So, it's a proportional reasoning: more guards mean a bigger supermarket. This is similar to the context because it's about the number of guards (like the number of active ingredients) determining the size (like the effectiveness of the antibiotic). So, more guards (like more ingredients) lead to better security (like better effectiveness). This seems to mirror the idea that more components make the system more robust, just like more ingredients make antibiotics more effective.\n\nOption D: This is about electric current and wire diameter. It says that a thicker wire carries more electricity because the flow is larger. This is a scientific principle, not a reasoning about group vs. individual. It's more about physics than logical reasoning, so it doesn't fit the context.\n\nPutting it all together, the context is about the difficulty in satisfying a group (like bacteria or guests) versus an individual. The best analogy is Option C, where the number of security guards (like active ingredients) determines the level of security (effectiveness). So, more guards mean a bigger supermarket, just as more ingredients mean a more effective antibiotic.\n</think>\n\nThe correct option is: C\n\nThe reasoning in the context highlights the challenge of satisfying a group (bacteria or guests) versus an individual. Option C mirrors this by showing that more security guards (active ingredients) are needed for a larger supermarket (more effective antibiotic), establishing a proportional relationship similar to the argument.\n\nThe correct option is: C",
