e patient's actual ability, that might not be hospice care.\n\nSo the answer should be A because it's about extending life, which isn't the focus of hospice care.\n</think>\n\nThe correct option is: A\n\nThe reasoning is that hospice care focuses on improving quality of life and comfort, not necessarily extending life. Option A involves aggressive treatment aimed at extending life, which doesn't align with the definition of hospice care.\n\nThe correct option is: A",
