ies that parents are still using various criteria, which might indicate a need for a balanced view of marriage beyond just material comforts. So D seems plausible.\n\nWait, but the context doesn't explicitly talk about a correct view of marriage, just that parents are using certain factors. Maybe D is about understanding that marriage isn't just about money but also about other aspects like affection and personal values. So D might be the intended conclusion.\n\nI think the key point is that the passage is highlighting that money is still a significant factor, so the conclusion should reflect that a correct view of marriage includes more than just financial aspects. So D makes sense.\n</think>\n\nThe correct option is: D) In order to have a good marriage, we should have a correct view of marriage and attitude towards marriage.",
