re not both in the first (they're in the second).\n     - A and C are not in the same formation (A in second, C in second).\n     - Aircraft carrier (assumed to be in second) is present.\n\n4. **Case 2: D is in the second formation.**\n   - If D is in the second, B must also be there (condition 4).\n   - Second formation: D, B, plus two others.\n   - First formation would have A, C, E, H, G minus those in second.\n   - However, this setup violates condition 4 if B is in the first, which it's not in this case. But since D is in the second, B must be there, making this scenario invalid because it would require B to be in both first and second, which isn't possible.\n\n5. **Conclusion:**\n   - Only Case 1 is valid, where B is in the first formation.\n\n**Answer:** B) B in the first formation.",
