      "text": "<think>\nOkay, so I need to figure out which of the options A, B, C, or D represents direct selling based on the given context. Let me start by understanding what direct selling is. From the context, direct selling is when a company recruits sellers who then sell products directly to consumers without going through intermediaries like retailers. So, the key here is that the product is sold directly to the end consumer, not through a middleman.\n\nNow, let's go through each option one by one.\n\nOption A: A dairy manufacturer set up 100 sales points in the city to sell dairy products at a unified price after selecting salesmen. Hmm, so they have sales points, which are physical locations. That sounds like they're selling directly through these points, which are probably acting as intermediaries. So this might not be direct selling because the product is being sold through these sales points, which are like branches or retailers.\n\nOption B: A bookstore adopts online sales. After customers place an order, the courier sends the products to the designated place and charges a fee. Wait, this is online sales, but the bookstore is the one delivering. So the customers are buying from the bookstore, which is an intermediary. So this isn't direct selling either because the bookstore is the middleman between the customer and the manufacturer.\n\nOption C: Some salesmen recruited by a cosmetics brand set up stalls along the road to distribute product descriptions and sell them to customers at lower prices. Here, the salesmen are directly selling the products to customers at lower prices. There's no mention of any intermediary like a retailer or wholesaler. So this seems like direct selling because the product is being sold directly to consumers through the salesmen.\n\nOption D: At the beginning of school, the new student Xie bought five table lamps in the wholesale market, one for his own use, and the other four were sold to his classmates. So, he bought from a wholesale market, which is an intermediary. He sold to his classmates, but the initial purchase was through a wholesale market, making it indirect. So this isn't direct selling.\n\nPutting it all together, the only option where the product is sold directly to consumers without intermediaries is Option C.\n</think>\n\nThe correct option is: C\n\nThe correct option is: C",
