\nD) Villagers who would have died from a virus were cured by a serum from a local flower that comes from the spotted bat. This suggests that the spotted bat's presence is linked to a cure, meaning the virus isn't as dangerous anymore. So, cutting the bat might mean the virus isn't a problem, which would actually help the government's goal. So this option supports the plan, not undermines it.\n\nSo, the best option is A because it directly ties the spotted bat's reservoir role to the majority of deaths. If the government cuts the bat, the main cause of death (the viruses from the spotted bat) would still be present, so deaths wouldn't decrease. Therefore, the plan won't achieve its objective.\n</think>\n\nThe correct option is: A\n\nThe reasoning is that if the spotted fruit bat is the only reservoir for deadly viruses causing most deaths, eliminating the bat won't reduce these deaths. \n\nAnswer: The correct option is: A",
