king for half a year, so he might not be using the necessary machinery and equipment, leading to inefficiency. This fits the boundary problem description because his short-term contract caused him to act in a short-sighted way, ignoring important tools.\n\nSo, putting it all together, the boundary problem is about short-term focus due to short employment periods. Option D clearly shows this by mentioning the half-year contract leading to ignoring machinery use, which is a short-sighted behavior.\n</think>\n\nThe correct option is: D\n\nThe correct option is: D",
