l market.\" The context mentions that China's green tea is distributed in mountainous areas and has a comparative advantage due to their resources. This suggests that Chinese green tea does have competitive strength. So this seems consistent.\n\nOption D: \"There is a trend of change red to green in the international tea market.\" The context says that countries like India, Indonesia, and Sri Lanka tried to switch from red (black) to green tea but failed. It doesn't mention a trend, just that their attempts failed. So this might not be correct.\n\nWait, but the context does say that the three countries changed red to green, but it ended in failure. So maybe the trend isn't a general trend but specific to those countries. The question is about the international market trend. The original text doesn't talk about a general trend, just that their attempts failed. So maybe D isn't correct.\n\nSo, putting it all together, the correct answer should be C because the context supports that Chinese green tea has competitive strength.\n</think>\n\nThe correct option is: C",
