mber of houses. It's more about a single discovery rather than a broader social pattern. So this option doesn't support the point either.\n\nOption D: Only when ceremonial activities are held will the ornaments of processed antlers appear. The context mentions that ornaments of processed antlers were found, indicating ceremonial activities. This seems to support the idea that ceremonial activities were present, which aligns with the point of view in the context. It suggests that the presence of antler ornaments is a sign of such activities, which the context already mentions.\n\nSo, putting it all together, Option D directly supports the point of view by linking the presence of antler ornaments to ceremonial activities, which is a key point in the context.\n</think>\n\nThe correct option is: D\n\nThe reasoning is that Option D directly supports the context by linking the presence of antler ornaments to ceremonial activities, which is a key point mentioned in the context.\n\nThe correct option is: D",
