      "text": "<think>\nOkay, so I need to figure out which company David should choose based on the given options. Let me start by understanding the problem step by step.\n\nFirst, the context says that David is a senior CEO looking for a company with the best treatment. Huizhong and Cantor are the two options. Both companies offer similar terms except for salary and its increases. I need to compare these two offers to see which one is better for David.\n\nLet me break down the details:\n\nHuizhong Company:\n- Salary: Half-yearly salary of $500,000.\n- Increase: $50,000 every half-year.\n\nCantor Company:\n- Salary: Annual salary of $1,000,000.\n- Increase: $200,000 annually.\n\nWait, that's a bit confusing. Let me make sure I understand the timing. Huizhong pays every half-year, so every six months, while Cantor pays once a year. The increases are also on different schedules.\n\nI think I should calculate the total salary over a specific period, say two years, to compare both companies. That way, I can see the total amount David would receive from each company and determine which is better.\n\nLet's start with Huizhong:\n\nHuizhong:\n- First half-year: $500,000\n- Second half-year: $500,000 + $50,000 = $550,000\n- Third half-year: $550,000 + $50,000 = $600,000\n- Fourth half-year: $600,000 + $50,000 = $650,000\n\nWait, but two years would be four half-years. So adding them up:\n\nTotal for Huizhong over two years:\n$500,000 + $550,000 + $600,000 + $650,000 = Let's add them step by step.\n\nFirst two half-years: $500,000 + $550,000 = $1,050,000\nNext two half-years: $600,000 + $650,000 = $1,250,000\nTotal: $1,050,000 + $1,250,000 = $2,300,000\n\nNow, Cantor:\n\nCantor:\n- First year: $1,000,000\n- Second year: $1,000,000 + $200,000 = $1,200,000\n\nTotal for Cantor over two years: $1,000,000 + $1,200,000 = $2,200,000\n\nWait, so over two years, Huizhong gives David $2,300,000, while Cantor gives $2,200,000. So Huizhong is better by $100,000 over two years. But let m