      "text": "<think>\nOkay, so I need to figure out which option belongs to field dependence based on the given definition. Let me start by understanding what field dependence means. From the context provided, field dependence refers to individuals who rely heavily on external references for processing information. This makes it difficult for them to ignore the influence of their environment, especially people around them, like authorities. They tend to observe words and emotions closely, paying attention to social content in verbal messages.\n\nNow, looking at the options:\n\nA) Have the ability to learn independently. This seems more about internal motivation and self-reliance. People with this ability don't need external factors to learn, so it doesn't fit field dependence.\n\nB) Have one's own opinion on the evaluation of others. This involves personal judgment and self-perception influenced by others. Since field dependence is about being easily influenced by the environment, especially people, this might fit. They might rely on others' opinions more than their own.\n\nC) Doing things is dominated by intrinsic motivation. Intrinsic motivation is about internal drive, so this is the opposite of field dependence, which is external.\n\nD) Doing things is dominated by external motivation. Wait, field dependence is about being influenced by external factors, so this seems to align. But I need to think carefully. The definition says it's difficult to get rid of environmental influence, so external factors are dominant in their processing. So D might be the correct answer.\n\nWait, but the question is asking which option belongs to field dependence. Let me re-read the options. Option B is about having their own opinion on others' evaluation, which is influenced by others, so that's external. Option D is about doing things being dominated by external motivation, which also fits because field dependents are influenced by external factors.\n\nHmm, I'm a bit confused. Let me clarify. Field dependence is about being influenced by the environment, especially people. So if someone's actions are dominated by external factors, that's field dependence. So D would be correct because their behavior is driven by external influences.\n\nBut wait, the question is about which option belongs to field dependence. So the correct answer should reflect that their behavior is influenced by external factors. So D seems to fit because it's about being dominated by external motivation.\n\nAlternatively, B is about their self-perception being influenced by others, which is also external. So both B and D might seem relevant, but I think the key is that field dependence is about processing information influenced by the environment, which affects their behavior. So D directly states that their actions are dominated by external factors, which aligns with field dependence.\n\nI think I'll go with D as the correct answer.\n</think>\n\nThe correct option is: D\n\nThe correct option is: D",
