ut the trend of losing lab experiments leading to students not knowing how to work with equipment. Option B shows that some schools are still doing labs, which means the trend isn't as severe as the argument claims. Therefore, it weakens the argument by providing a counterexample that the trend isn't as bad as feared.\n</think>\n\nThe correct option is: B\n\nThe reasoning is that option B shows that some secondary schools still conduct laboratory experiments, indicating that the trend of replacing them with computer simulations isn't as widespread as the argument suggests. This directly weakens the argument by providing evidence that lab work is still occurring in some schools.\n\nThe correct option is: B",
