fore, this option is incorrect because it's the opposite of what's stated.\n\nSo, putting it all together, the only inference we can make is that Zhang Fei had a mind and accepted new ideas, which is option B.\n</think>\n\nThe correct option is: B\n\nStep-by-step explanation:\n1. The context indicates that historically, only boys in the countryside had access to education.\n2. Zhang Fei successfully entered university, which required intellectual capability and openness to new ideas.\n3. Therefore, it can be inferred that Zhang Fei had a mind and accepted new ideas.\n\nThe correct option is: B",
