ted at all. That makes it a strong argument against the engineer's reasoning. Option A also supports the idea that air quality isn't the issue because it works well elsewhere, which is another way to refute the engineer's point.\n\nI think both A and C are good, but C is more about the possibility that air quality isn't the main issue, while A shows that it's not the only issue. But since the question is about refuting the engineer's argument, which is that poor air quality is the cause, C is more about showing that air quality isn't the only factor, making the engineer's reasoning weaker. So I think C is the best answer.\n</think>\n\nThe correct option is: C",
