      "text": "<think>\nOkay, so I'm trying to figure out this question about the meaning of \"contextual\" in the given paragraph. Let me read the context again carefully. The paragraph says that rural culture is a system determined by the society's production and living conditions, and that importing advanced culture from outside isn't realistic. \n\nThe question is asking which option best explains what \"contextual\" means here. The options are A, B, C, D. Let me break them down one by one.\n\nOption A says \"Adapted to the experience of production and life in various parts of the countryside.\" Hmm, that sounds like it's talking about how rural areas have their own production and life experiences. But the paragraph mentions that importing advanced culture isn't realistic, so maybe it's more about how rural culture is self-contained rather than adapting to different areas.\n\nOption B is \"Adapting to the actual development and changes in rural areas.\" This seems related to the idea of fitting into the existing environment, but I'm not sure if it's exactly what \"contextual\" means here. The paragraph doesn't specifically mention development or changes, just that importing advanced culture doesn't fit.\n\nOption C states \"Connected with and integrated with the reality of the local rural society.\" This makes sense because the paragraph talks about rural culture being determined by their own production and living conditions, which are part of their reality. So, contextual here probably means it's integrated with their actual reality.\n\nOption D says \"Adapted to the development of advanced culture.\" But the paragraph clearly says that importing advanced culture is not realistic, so this doesn't fit. It's the opposite of what's being stated.\n\nPutting it all together, the paragraph emphasizes that rural culture is self-contained and doesn't rely on external influences. So the best answer is C, which connects the rural culture with their own reality.\n</think>\n\nThe correct option is: C\n\nThe paragraph emphasizes that rural culture is shaped by its own production and living conditions, making it integrated with the local rural society's reality. Therefore, the most accurate understanding of \"contextual\" is that it is connected with and integrated with the reality of the local rural society.\n\nThe correct option is: C",
