\n\nC1: Zhao Ming \u2192 Peking (unknown yet)\nC2: Sun Jie \u2192 Tsinghua (but Sun Jie is Beijing Normal, so C2 is wrong. Therefore, C1 must be correct. So Zhao Ming is Peking.\n\nSo now, we have:\n\nZhao Ming: Peking\nQian Hong: Tsinghua\nSun Jie: Beijing Normal\n\nLet me check if this fits all the conditions.\n\nChecking A's guesses:\n- A1: Zhao Ming \u2192 Tsinghua (wrong)\n- A2: Sun Jie \u2192 Beijing Normal (correct)\nSo A has one correct, one wrong. Good.\n\nChecking B's guesses:\n- B1: Zhao Ming \u2192 Beijing Normal (wrong)\n- B2: Qian Hong \u2192 Tsinghua (correct)\nSo B has one correct, one wrong. Good.\n\nChecking C's guesses:\n- C1: Zhao Ming \u2192 Peking (correct)\n- C2: Sun Jie \u2192 Tsinghua (wrong)\nSo C has one correct, one wrong. Good.\n\nSo this seems to fit all the conditions. Now, let's look at the options.\n\nOption A: Zhao Ming Peking, Qian Hong Tsinghua, Sun Jie Beijing Normal. That's exactly what we have. So Option A is correct.\n\nWait, but let me check the other options to make sure.\n\nOption B: Zhao Ming Tsinghua, Qian Hong Beijing Normal, Sun Jie Peking. But we determined Sun Jie is Beijing Normal, so this can't be right.\n\nOption C: Zhao Ming Beijing Normal, Qian Hong Tsinghua, Sun Jie Peking. No, because Sun Jie is Beijing Normal.\n\nOption D: Zhao Ming Peking, Qian Hong Beijing Normal, Sun Jie Tsinghua. No, because Sun Jie is Beijing Normal, and Qian Hong is Tsinghua, but Sun Jie can't be Tsinghua.\n\nSo the correct answer is Option A.\n</think>\n\nThe correct option is: A\n\nThe correct admission is:\nZhao Ming \u2192 Peking University\nQian Hong \u2192 Tsinghua University\nSun Jie \u2192 Beijing Normal University\n\nThe correct option is: A\n\nThe correct option is: A\n\nThe correct option is: A\n\nThe correct option is: A\n\nThe correct option is: A\n\nThe correct option is: A\n\nThe correct option is: A\n\nThe correct option is: A\n\nThe correct option is: A\n\nThe correct option is: A\n\nThe correct option is: A\n\nThe corre