      "text": "<think>\nOkay, so I need to figure out which option the paragraph is trying to make. Let me read the context again carefully. \n\nThe paragraph talks about an oil exploration team in Mexico's Gocatan Peninsula finding a huge crater. Most of it is submerged near the Yucatan Peninsula, with a width of 160 to 240 kilometers. The age of the sediment suggests the crater was formed about 65 million years ago, which is when the dinosaurs went extinct. So, the discovery supports the idea that the impact of a meteorite caused the extinction.\n\nNow, looking at the options:\n\nA) Before 1990, no one thought dinosaurs died from meteorites. The paragraph mentions that before 1990, the team stumbled upon the crater, but it doesn't say that no one thought meteorites were responsible before then. It just says they found evidence, which led to the consensus.\n\nB) The discovery made scientists more consistent with the cause. The paragraph says the discovery basically reached a consensus, so this seems to fit. It supports the idea more, making it more consistent.\n\nC) Dinosaurs were around 65 million years ago. The paragraph mentions the crater was formed then, but it doesn't say anything about the density of dinosaurs. It just states the time frame, so this might not be the main point.\n\nD) The crash is a natural phenomenon. The paragraph doesn't talk about whether it's natural or not; it just states the event. So this isn't the main point.\n\nSo, the main point is that the discovery supported the cause of dinosaur extinction, making B the correct answer.\n</think>\n\nThe paragraph discusses the discovery of a crater linked to the dinosaurs' extinction, suggesting it was caused by a meteorite impact. This supports the consensus among scientists about the cause.\n\nThe correct option is: B",
