issue of gold plating or the survey data provided.\n\nPutting it all together, Option B seems to directly address the lack of knowledge about the job market, which would hinder their ability to find employment despite their studies abroad. The other options either don't explain the job search issue as clearly or are more about specific groups (like high-achieving graduates).\n</think>\n\nThe correct option is: B\n\nThe correct option is: B",
