      "text": "<think>\nOkay, so I'm trying to figure out this question about mice exposed to radiation and their likelihood of developing leukemia. Let me start by reading the context carefully.\n\nThere are 200 mice, all the same kind, and none had leukemia to begin with. They were all exposed to the same kind of radiation with the same dose and intensity. Then, half of them were given their normal food, and the other half were given limited food. After some time, 55 mice in the group that ate normal food developed leukemia, while only 3 in the limited food group did.\n\nThe question is asking which of the four options is correct based on this information. Let me go through each option one by one.\n\nOption A says that whether exposed to radiation or not, letting mice eat normally increases the likelihood of leukemia. Hmm, wait. The context says that the mice were exposed to radiation, so the exposure is a given. The difference is in their diet. The group with normal food had 55 cases, and the limited food had 3. So, actually, giving normal food increased leukemia cases. So A might not be correct because it's not about exposure; it's about the food. Plus, the exposure is the same for both groups.\n\nOption B claims that leukemia isn't related to radiation exposure. But the data shows that the group exposed to radiation had higher leukemia rates, especially in the normal food group. So B is definitely wrong because it directly contradicts the results.\n\nOption C states that controlling the amount of food reduces the likelihood of leukemia from radiation. That makes sense because the limited food group had fewer cases (3) compared to the normal food group (55). So controlling the food intake seems to have a protective effect against leukemia in this context. So C looks correct.\n\nOption D says that mice exposed to radiation will definitely develop leukemia. But in the study, only 55 out of 200 developed it, which is a high number but not all. So D is incorrect because it's not a certainty; it's just a higher risk.\n\nSo putting it all together, the correct answer should be C because limiting the food intake reduced leukemia cases among the radiation-exposed mice.\n</think>\n\nThe correct option is: C\n\nThe study shows that mice exposed to radiation had higher leukemia rates when given normal food, but controlling their food intake reduced leukemia cases. This indicates that limiting food can help reduce leukemia risk from radiation exposure.\n\nThe correct option is: C",
