If half is both, then in those areas, neither is easy. So, if the original statement is true, then in most parts, at least one is easy. So, if half the country is both, then those parts are in the majority, which would make the original statement false. Therefore, A must be false.\n\nOption B: If most parts are cold, then in those parts, cyclamen can be grown easily, which fits the original statement. So B doesn't have to be false.\n\nOption C: If some parts are neither, that's okay because the original statement only requires that in most parts, at least one is easy. So C doesn't have to be false.\n\nOption D: If it's impossible to grow cyclamen, then in all parts, rice must be easy. But the original statement allows for some parts where neither is easy, as long as most parts have at least one. So, if D is true, then in all parts, rice is easy, which would make the original statement true because in all parts, rice is easy. But the original statement says \"in most parts,\" not all. So, D could be true or false, but it's not necessarily false.\n\nWait, but if D is true, then in all parts, cyclamen can't be grown, so in all parts, rice must be easy. But the original statement says that in most parts, at least one is easy. So, if in all parts, rice is easy, then the original statement is true because in all parts, at least one is easy. So, D being true doesn't contradict the original statement. Therefore, D doesn't have to be false.\n\nSo, the only option that must be false is A because if half the country is both dry and hot, then in those parts, neither is easy, which would mean that in the majority of parts, neither is easy, contradicting the original statement.\n</think>\n\nThe correct option is: A\n\nStep-by-step explanation:\n\n1. The original statement says that in most parts, either cyclamen or rice is easy to grow.\n2. If half the country is both dry and hot (Option A), those areas would make neither easy to grow.\n3. Since \"most parts\" require at least one to be easy, Option A contradicts the original statement.\n4. Therefore, Option A must be false.\n\nThe correct option is: A",
