      "text": "<think>\nOkay, so I need to figure out which option the paragraph is explaining. Let me read the context again carefully.\n\nThe paragraph starts by talking about how increased meat production affects the greenhouse effect. It mentions that animal husbandry currently uses 30% of the earth's land area and is one of the fastest-growing agricultural sectors. It also notes that in Latin America, 70% of forests have been cut down for pastures. Additionally, it states that animal husbandry threatens 306 out of 825 terrestrial ecosystems and 1699 endangered species.\n\nSo, the main points are about the environmental impact of animal husbandry, specifically how it uses up land, disrupts ecosystems, and endangers species. It's all about the negative effects on the environment.\n\nLooking at the options:\n\nA) The environmental cost of developing animal husbandry. This seems relevant because the paragraph discusses how animal husbandry uses land and affects ecosystems and species, which are all environmental costs.\n\nB) The development of animal husbandry should be strictly controlled. The paragraph doesn't explicitly say this, but it does imply that animal husbandry is a problem, so controlling its development might be a solution. However, it's more about explaining the problem than recommending control.\n\nC) Bottleneck in the development of animal husbandry. There's no mention of a bottleneck; the paragraph talks about land use and threats, not about a lack of resources or capacity.\n\nD) Serious pollution caused by animal husbandry. The paragraph doesn't specifically mention pollution, but it does talk about land use and habitat destruction, which can lead to pollution indirectly. However, the main focus is more on habitat and biodiversity than directly on pollution.\n\nSo, the paragraph is mainly explaining the environmental cost, which is option A. It's not about pollution specifically, so D is less likely. It's also not about controlling development, so