n't say anything about other revenue sources. So maybe the airport's total expenses are higher than just the user fees. But the question is about what must be true. If the user fees didn't bring in enough, and the airport still needs to cover all expenses, then the expenses must be greater than the user fees. So D is correct.\n\nI think D is the right answer because it's the only one that directly relates to the given information without assuming anything not stated.\n</think>\n\nThe correct option is: D\n\nStep-by-step explanation:\n\n1. The airport's operating expenses include all sources of revenue, not just user fees.\n2. The user fees collected were lower than expected.\n3. Therefore, the total operating expenses must be greater than the revenue from user fees alone.\n\nAnswer: D",
